#Mini Project

#Project Description

This project integrates a two-wheel motor control system with a computer vision interface using a Raspberry Pi and Arduino. 
A camera detects the position of a visual marker within four image quadrants, and the marker location is used to command independent 
target positions for the left and right wheels. The system also implements PI position control so the motors return to their commanded 
positions after disturbances, while an LCD displays the current goal positions.

